  "question": {
    "text": "<p>If the solubility product of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AB</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, then the solubility of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>AB</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in pure water is _______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>[Assuming that neither kind of ion reacts with water]</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable equalrows=\"true\" equalcolumns=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>AB</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mover><mo>&#8652;</mo><mrow/></mover></mtd><mtd><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>+</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd/><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mtd><mtd/><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi>sp</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.20</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>So solubility&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi>mol</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  }
